e B\", \"Brasileirão Série C\"]\n\n    if \"copa do brasil\" in q or \"brazilian cup\" in q:\n        return [\"Copa do Brasil\"]\n\n    return None\n\n\ndef _to_int(series: pd.Series) -> pd.Series:\n    return pd.to_numeric(series, errors=\"coerce\").astype(\"Int64\")","lineStart":220,"lineEnd":339,"totalLines":944,"truncated":true}},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/knowledge_graph.py","time":{"start":1782351408486,"end":1782351408493}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Need move normalize_text and helpers before CANONICAL. Let's extract function definitions and place before CANONICAL. Use edit: replace the block from line 66 onward. We can cut-paste. Easier: Edit file to insert normalize_text and helpers before CANONICAL and remove duplicates. Since file large, maybe rewrite? We can do targeted edits.\n\nSimpler: Move the normalization block: insert functions after PREFIXES and before CANONICAL comment, then remove original function definitions after alias normalization. Let's use edit. First insert before line 66 comment. Then remove lines 198-? duplicates.\n\nBut functions are defined at line 198-... and used at line 195 before defined. If we move them before, line 195 works. Then there will be duplicate definitions later. Need remove duplicates. Let's see where duplicate ends. Use read more.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc6c297500179JyJmYSRdSaJV","sessionID":"ses_1039ff019ffe12Z8126LKUxZU8","messageID":"msg_efc6c0d2f001gnITpBzqKhD6W8"}}
