ext":"BR-Football has matches on adjacent days with same teams/goals? For example 2022-06-11 Corinthians vs ... same as Brasileirao? Actually the dates differ by one day (BR-Football date off by one) and goals maybe same? So dedup by date didn't catch. We need deduplicate by competition+season+home_canonical+away_canonical+round? But BR-Football lacks round. Could dedup by competition+season+home_canonical+away_canonical (ignoring date and goals), keeping first source priority. That would eliminate BR-Football duplicates when Brasileirao_Matches has same fixture. But could also remove legitimate matches where same teams play twice in a season? In a round-robin league, teams play each other twice (home/away). So home+away canonical pair appears twice per season (once each venue). If we dedup by competition+season+home_canonical+away_canonical, we'd reduce to one match per pair, losing the return fixture. Need include home/away direction, so pair appears twice (one home each). In a 20-team league, each pair has two matches, one in each half. Dedup by (competition, season, home_canonical, away_canonical) would keep both because home/away swapped for return fixture. That is correct. For two-legged cups, same pair could appear more than twice with same home/away? In a knockout, two legs: home/away swapped. So (home,away) unique per leg. But if datasets duplicate same leg, dedup by (competition, season, home, away) would catch. However, what about Libertadores group stage where teams play home and away once each? Home/away swapped. Good.\n\nBut within a league, a pair may play twice in same season with same home team? No. So dedup by competition+season+home_canonical+away_canonical is safe for league/cup group. For cup knockout two legs, home/away swapped; safe. For finals single match, safe.\n\nBut the BR-Football duplicates have same home/away as Brasileirao but different date/goals? Actually the date differs by one day and maybe goals same or different. Dedup by pair would catch. But if goals differ, which is correct? We can prefer Brasileirao_Matches for Brasileirão and Copa data? Maybe set source priority: official match files first, BR-Football lower. For each (competition, season, home_canonical, away_canonical), keep the row from the highest-priority source. This will deduplicate and prefer more authoritative source.\n\nSource priority:\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv for Brasileirão\n- Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv for Copa do Brasil\n- Libertadores_Matches.csv for Copa Libertadores\n- novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv for Brasileirão 2003-2019 (but overlaps with Brasileirao_Matches 2012-2019). Which prefer? The Brasileirao_Matches likely more consistent. But novo has stadium info. Could use source priority: official > extended. For same pair, choose Brasileirao_Matches over BR-Football and novo.\n- BR-Football-Dataset.csv lowest priority.\n\nImplement: assign `source_priority` numeric; sort by priority ascending; drop duplicates subset `['competition','season','home_canonical','away_canonical']` keep first. But this may remove legitimate return fixtures? No because home/away swapped. For double round-robin, pair with swapped home/away is a different subset, kept. Good.\n\nHowever, for BR-Football which includes Serie B/C, no overlap. For Libertadores, no overlap. For Copa do Brasil, BR-Football also includes Copa do Brasil and may overlap with Brazilian_Cup_Matches. Dedup by pair will handle.\n\nWhat about a cup where same teams meet in different rounds (home same, away same) in same season? In a knockout, they meet at most once per leg with home/away swapped. In group stage, same pair plays twice with home swapped. So same (home,away) not repeated in same season. Unless there is a one-off final neutral ground not in data. Safe.\n\nFor `novo` vs `Brasileirao_Matches`, both have same pair with same home/away for 2012-2019. We prefer Brasileirao_Matches. But novo has stadium info; losing. Could instead keep both but dedup by date? Many dates differ? Let's see. The official matches likely same dates. Our earlier Flamengo 2019 from novo had 2 rows maybe duplicates not matched. If we prefer Brasileirao_Matches, we drop novo duplicates. Good.\n\nBut note: novo covers 2003-2011 where Brasileirao_Matches doesn't. So kept.\n\nLet's implement priority sort and drop duplicates by ['competition','season','home_canonical','away_canonical'].\n\nSource priority dict:\n```\npriority = {\n    'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 1,\n    'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv': 1,\n    'Libertadores_Matches.csv': 1,\n    'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 2,\n    'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 3,\n}\n```\nUse after derived columns. Then drop duplicates.\n\nLet's test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc703a9b0019GFBUHv30MGlm6","sessionID":"ses_1039ff019ffe12Z8126LKUxZU8","messageID":"msg_efc6fe4b8001OMmbCwifd781TX"}}
