ader and normalization","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement query functions (matches, teams, players, competitions, stats)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement MCP server with FastMCP tools","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write tests covering required behaviors","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run tests and fix any issues","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Verify build/install and server starts","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}],"truncated":false},"title":"3 todos","time":{"start":1782351808662,"end":1782351808668}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now write tests. Use pytest. Test both knowledge graph functions and server tool functions.\n\nNeed tests for:\n- Data loads, all 6 CSVs loaded.\n- list_competitions includes expected competitions.\n- search_matches: Palmeiras 2023 returns matches with date, scores, competition.\n- search_matches: Copa do Brasil finals? Maybe just competition filter returns matches.\n- head-to-head: Flamengo vs Fluminense returns record.\n- team_stats: Corinthians home 2022 has Matches and win rate.\n- standings: 2019 Flamengo champion with 90 pts.\n- top_scoring_teams returns non-empty.\n- biggest_wins returns non-empty.\n- average_goals returns values.\n- search_players: Brazilian players includes Neymar Jr.\n- search_players: Gabriel Barbosa by name? Data doesn't contain Gabriel Barbosa. Maybe test search by name \"Neymar\".\n- player search by club Flamengo returns empty (since FIFA no Brazilian clubs). We can still assert empty.\n- list_seasons.\n\nAlso test normalization: display_name handles variants.\n\nPerformance tests maybe not needed.\n\nWrite tests/test_soccer_mcp.py. Use fixtures maybe. Since kg loads once, module-level fixture.\n\nNeed ensure tests don't call FastMCP server network. We can test server tool functions by importing functions.\n\nMaybe also test server lists tools. But calling list_tools might be okay. We'll test `mcp.list_tools()`? FastMCP has method. It returns list. But we can skip.\n\nLet's write tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc7240ac00177b8bDPCtYhlt5","sessionID":"ses_1039ff019ffe12Z8126LKUxZU8","messageID":"msg_efc7220fe001obsJULJGxd8D6z"}}
