{"type":"text","timestamp":1782352022931,"sessionID":"ses_1039ff019ffe12Z8126LKUxZU8","part":{"id":"prt_efc757af9001DbUSGiWMgxx7nn","messageID":"msg_efc7565be001M2nakuisodfGV7","sessionID":"ses_1039ff019ffe12Z8126LKUxZU8","type":"text","text":"Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server per `TASK.md`.\n\n**Files created:**\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__init__.py`\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/knowledge_graph.py` — loads all 6 CSVs, normalizes team names/dates/competitions, deduplicates overlapping sources, and exposes query methods.\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/server.py` — FastMCP server with tools for matches, head-to-head, team stats, standings, top scorers, biggest wins, averages, competitions, seasons, and players.\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__main__.py` — `python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp` stdio entry point.\n- `pyproject.toml` — build metadata and dependencies.\n- `tests/test_soccer_mcp.py` — 18 pytest tests covering data loading, normalization, match/team/competition/player queries, and MCP tools.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `python3 -m pytest tests -q` → **18 passed**\n- Built successfully: `python3 -m pip wheel . --no-deps -w dist`\n- Server starts and responds to MCP initialize over stdio.\n\nThe server handles team-name variations (e.g., `Flamengo-RJ`, `Clube de Regatas do Flamengo`, `Athletico Paranaense` vs `Atlético-MG`), multiple date formats, UTF-8 Portuguese text, and cross-file queries.","time":{"start":1782352018169,"end":1782352022907}}}
